From: Richard Spindler <richard@lateralblast.com.au>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 32/55] hpnsshd_config.5: say that DisableMTAES covers only
 AES-CTR

DisableMTAES switches the multithreaded AES-CTR cipher back to the stock one.
It does not touch the multithreaded ChaCha20-Poly1305 cipher, which the server
picks when chacha20-poly1305-mt@hpnssh.org is in Ciphers and the client
chooses ChaCha20-Poly1305, so a reader who set DisableMTAES could expect both
to be off. Say so, and say how to keep the serial ChaCha.
---
 hpnsshd_config.5 | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hpnsshd_config.5 b/hpnsshd_config.5
index 01fae5add..df243544a 100644
--- a/hpnsshd_config.5
+++ b/hpnsshd_config.5
@@ -733,6 +733,13 @@ simplify restricted configurations.
 Switch the encryption cipher being used from the multithreaded MT-AES-CTR cipher
 back to the stock single-threaded AES-CTR cipher. Default is 
 .Cm no. HPNSSH only. 
+It affects only the AES-CTR cipher. The multithreaded ChaCha20-Poly1305 cipher
+is used when
+.Cm chacha20-poly1305-mt@hpnssh.org
+is in
+.Cm Ciphers
+and the client chooses ChaCha20-Poly1305; to keep the serial cipher, leave that name out of
+.Cm Ciphers .
 .It Cm ExposeAuthInfo
 Writes a temporary file containing a list of authentication methods and
 public credentials (e.g. keys) used to authenticate the user.
